{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "godunov_norm_2d_eikonal_dirichlet_mms",
    "description": "Method-of-manufactured-solutions order-of-accuracy driver for grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/godunov_norm_D2_dirichlet_bc on the unit box [0,1]x[0,1] with inhomogeneous DIRICHLET (state-constraint) boundaries on all four walls, the Dirichlet companion of problems/godunov_norm_2d_eikonal_mms.esm (doubly-periodic) and the 2-D companion of godunov_norm_1d_eikonal_dirichlet_mms. Forced-steady eikonal u_t = -S|grad u| + S|grad g| with the manufactured solution g(x,y) = 0.5 + sin(pi x) sin(pi y): because u_t = -S|grad g| + S|grad g| = 0, g is the EXACT solution of the continuous forced PDE for all t, so the analytic reference at every time is g. The forcing S|grad g| = S pi sqrt(cos^2(pi x) sin^2(pi y) + sin^2(pi x) cos^2(pi y)) balances the operator. Discretely u_t = S*(|grad g| - godunov(u)); the imbalance is the first-order Godunov truncation S*(|grad g| - godunov(g)) = O(dx + dy), so ||u(T) - g|| = O(h) -- expected order 1. The chosen g is CONSTANT (= 0.5) on all four walls (sin(pi x) = 0 at x = 0, 1 and sin(pi y) = 0 at y = 0, 1), so the prescribed constant-along-wall Dirichlet free names are gL = gR = gB = gT = 0.5 (nonzero, matched; homogeneous case is 0). g is antisymmetric about each wall (sin(pi x) is odd about x = 0 and about x = 1), so the antisymmetric mirror ghost 2*g_wall - u reproduces g's true smooth extension across every wall and the edge/corner faces converge at the same order-1 rate as the interior -- a clean order-1 gate with nothing to exempt (unlike a doubly-periodic ramp, which is a contradiction). THE KINKS ARE NOT A PROBLEM: |grad g| has slope-sign kinks where each gradient component changes sign and a norm cusp at the interior extremum (1/2,1/2) where grad g vanishes, yet the per-axis Rouy-Tourin/Osher-Sethian entropy fix selects the correct one-sided branch, so the scheme stays first order in L2 AND Linf. EXACTNESS: the operator annihilates a constant field exactly (null-space |grad const| = 0) and, because every wall trace of g is the constant 0.5, the mirror-ghost closure is compatible with the scalar wall values (a general non-constant affine field would have wall traces varying along each wall, out of scope for scalar Dirichlet data). Geometry contract fulfilled for the unit box: x0 = y0 = 0, dx = 1/NX, dy = 1/NY. The ic, forcing, and test references spell x_i = (i - 1/2)/NX, y_j = (j - 1/2)/NY inline from literals and NX, NY (build-time scope-free). Per-resolution error norms pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/godunov_norm_2d_eikonal_dirichlet_mms/golden/errors.json.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "equation:hamilton_jacobi",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Rouy, E., & Tourin, A. (1992). A viscosity solutions approach to shape-from-shading. SIAM Journal on Numerical Analysis, 29(3), 867-884. Convergence of the monotone Godunov Hamiltonian to the viscosity solution of the eikonal equation at first order.",
        "doi": "10.1137/0729053"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Osher, S., & Sethian, J. A. (1988). Fronts propagating with curvature-dependent speed. Journal of Computational Physics, 79(1), 12-49. The upwind entropy construction of |grad phi| for level-set Hamilton-Jacobi terms.",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(88)90002-2"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.12 (cell-centered Dirichlet via mirror ghost)."
      },
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "GodunovEikonal2DDirichletMMS": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/godunov_norm_D2_dirichlet_bc.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "Level-set field integrated under the forced eikonal u_t = -S*godunov(u) + S|grad g|; starts at and stays near g(x,y) = 0.5 + sin(pi x) sin(pi y), deviating by the O(h) truncation error."
        },
        "S": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Non-negative Hamilton-Jacobi speed. The forcing carries the matching S so g is exact for any S > 0."
        },
        "gL": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.5,
          "description": "Prescribed value on the left x-wall x=x0 (rule Dirichlet free name), equal to the manufactured wall trace g(0,y) = 0.5 (constant along the wall)."
        },
        "gR": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.5,
          "description": "Prescribed value on the right x-wall x=x0+NX*dx, equal to g(1,y) = 0.5."
        },
        "gB": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.5,
          "description": "Prescribed value on the bottom y-wall y=y0, equal to g(x,0) = 0.5."
        },
        "gT": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.5,
          "description": "Prescribed value on the top y-wall y=y0+NY*dy, equal to g(x,1) = 0.5."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left x domain edge a = 0 (unit box): the grid's x0 free name."
        },
        "y0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Bottom y domain edge b = 0 (unit box): the grid's y0 free name."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "x-spacing 1/NX: the grid's dx free name. NX substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6)."
        },
        "dy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "y-spacing 1/NY: the grid's dy free name. NY substituted at load."
        },
        "forcing": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1/s",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "The manufactured source |grad g| = pi sqrt(cos^2(pi x_i) sin^2(pi y_j) + sin^2(pi x_i) cos^2(pi y_j)) (S folded via the du/dt scaling; x_i,y_j spelled inline). It balances the continuous operator so g is the steady exact solution; the residual is the O(h) truncation error."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i",
              "j"
            ],
            "args": [],
