      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_eikonal_dirichlet",
          "description": "Manufactured solution g(x,y) = 0.5 + sin(pi x) sin(pi y), S = 1, prescribed Dirichlet walls gL=gR=gB=gT=0.5 (the constant wall trace of g). u_t = -S|grad u| + S|grad g| with u(0) = g gives u_t = 0 continuously, so g is exact for all t; discretely u_t = S*(|grad g| - godunov(u)) and the imbalance is the truncation S*(|grad g| - godunov(g)) = O(h), so ||u(T) - g|| = O(h). g is antisymmetric about each wall so the mirror-ghost closure reproduces g's smooth extension and the edges/corners converge at order 1. References evaluate g at cell centers x_i = (i - 1/2)/NX, y_j = (j - 1/2)/NY inline per esm-spec 6.6.5. The t=0 assertion pins ic wiring (L2_error 0 within 1e-9); the t=0.2 assertion bounds the first-order error under the 0.1 cap. Exact per-resolution errors pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/godunov_norm_2d_eikonal_dirichlet_mms/golden/errors.json.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.2
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "i",
                  "j"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
